# SHA-256 of every migration file's bytes, one line per file, in the format
# `sha256sum` writes. This file is what makes "an applied migration is never
# edited" enforceable: `cargo xtask verify-migrations` (in `just verify` and in
# CI's self-checks job) fails when a file's hash moves.
#
# WHY: sqlx::migrate! stores a SHA-384 of each file's whole bytes in
# `_sqlx_migrations.checksum` and refuses to boot when a file no longer hashes
# to what the database recorded. PR #39 rewrote a comment inside
# 0028_create-checkout-sessions.sql after it shipped, and every database that
# had applied the original stopped booting (issue #76).
#
# To add a migration: `just migrations-manifest` appends its line. That recipe
# REFUSES to rewrite an existing line, so this file cannot be regenerated to
# silence the gate. To fix an applied migration, write a new one.
#
# Order does not matter. See backends/migrations/README.md and
# docs/runbooks/migrations.md.
